 ## Overview
-This method optimizes a transfer function $T_o$ for an optimization volume field $F_o$ such that its rendered images match those of a reference volume field $F_r$ rendered with a reference transfer function $T_r$ [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of finding a visual mapping for one dataset that reproduces the appearance of another, enabling comparative volume rendering [S1, unofficial]. It differs from voxel-based least-squares approaches by minimizing the difference between final rendered images rather than per-voxel color residuals, thereby prioritizing voxels that have a larger effect on the final image [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Differentiable Rendering and Sampling Methods](4973-differentiable-rendering-and-sampling-methods.md) by applying automatic differentiation to the direct volume rendering compositing equation.
